  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<section class=\"context\"><p>Two parallel conducting wires both of length 0.25 m are arranged 0.20 m apart in a circuit. The resistance of one wire is 15 Ω and the resistance of the other wire is 30 Ω. The current in the 15 Ω wire is 10 A.</p>\n<p>Assume that the magnetic force due to the Earth can be ignored.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> Determine the magnetic force acting on the 15 Ω wire due to the current in the 30 Ω wire. [4]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> </p><p>The magnetic field strength of Earth’s field at the location of the wires is 45 μT.</p>\n<p>Discuss the assumption made in this question.</p><p>[3]</p></section>"
  },
